# What the PYCUBED MISSION image is: the modules it executes in place,
# and the number of kernel processes it needs.
#
# See image-armv7minit for what these two facts mean and why there is
# one file per init.  doc/pycubed-plan.ms is the plan this image is
# phase 4 of; doc/radio-plan.ms is the radio under it.
#
# Four modules.  beepsatinit loads /dis/pycubed/beepsat.dis, which
# loads Sat and Hw; and the init itself loads Radiocal, to apply this
# board's crystal correction to the radio before the mission writes a
# packet to it.  Nothing else --
# no bufio, no string, no daytime, and no shell.  The hardware
# boundary is a directory of FILES (module/pycubedhw.m), so Hw is a
# parser and not a driver, and the drivers are in the kernel where
# this tree puts them.
XIPDIS=\
	pycubed/beepsat.dis\
	pycubed/sat.dis\
	pycubed/hw.dis\
	lib/radiocal.dis\


# Ten, and this is a first estimate to be measured rather than a
# figure from anywhere.
#
# beepsat spawns five: the state server and four tasks -- blink, time,
# vbatt and beacon -- and the init itself is a sixth.  The shell image
# runs two Dis processes at five slots, so five is certainly too few.
# Each slot is a 4096-byte kernel stack out of about 160K of RAM, which
# is why this cannot simply be set high: at nine a SHELL image could not
# run echo.  A mission image has no shell and therefore none of the
# shell's heap, which is the thing that made nine fail, so the trade
# here is different and has to be measured on the board.
NPROC=10

# The files this image carries that the conf's root section does not.
#
# dst then src, src relative to the tree root, which is the same pair a
# second field in the root section is.  The conf cannot hold these
# because every image built from it would carry them: the shell image
# would carry the mission's three modules and be unable to run them,
# which is exactly what it did until mkroot learned EXTRAROOT.
#
# /dis/pycubed is NOT named: mkroot builds the intermediate
# directories out of the paths themselves, and naming one as a pair
# gives an entry with a length and no data, which desyncs the generated
# root.s from the root.h beside it -- "root65len: not defined" at the
# link, which reads as a toolchain fault and is not one.
EXTRAROOT=\
	/dis/pycubed/beepsat.dis	/dis32/pycubed/beepsat.dis\
	/dis/pycubed/sat.dis		/dis32/pycubed/sat.dis\
	/dis/pycubed/hw.dis		/dis32/pycubed/hw.dis\
